Day 1/30 – Why Learn AWS?
🚀 Kickstarting my 30-day AWS journey with a question many beginners ask:

🔍 Why Should You Learn AWS Cloud?
💡 Because cloud is the future – and AWS is leading the way.

✅ Top Reasons to Learn AWS:
🔸 #1: Industry Leader
AWS is used by Netflix, NASA, Samsung, BMW, and countless startups. It holds over 30% of the cloud market share.

🔸 #2: In-Demand Skill
Cloud skills are one of the top 3 job requirements for tech roles in 2025 — especially AWS, which powers the infrastructure behind many apps and businesses.

🔸 #3: Huge Ecosystem
From hosting websites to building serverless apps, from data lakes to machine learning — AWS has 200+ services to explore.

🔸 #4: Beginner-Friendly
You can start with free-tier resources, hands-on labs, and real-time projects — no heavy setup needed!

🔸 #5: High Paying Jobs
Whether you're targeting DevOps, Cloud Engineer, or SRE roles — AWS expertise opens doors to high-paying global opportunities.

🔧 What You’ll Learn in This Series:
Every day, I’ll share:
✅ Powerful AWS concepts
✅ Key differences (IAM Roles vs Policies, EC2 vs Lambda, etc.)
✅ Mini project ideas
✅ Career tips and real-world use cases
